      "id": "phrase-por-ahi--around",
      "kind": "phrase",
      "promptEs": "por ahí",
      "questionEn": "How can you say that someone is somewhere around, or out and about, without naming an exact place?",
      "answerEn": "Use por ahí for a vague place or movement: “around,” “somewhere around there,” or “out and about.”",
      "noteEn": "Ahí normally points to a place away from the speaker. Adding por makes the location deliberately approximate and can suggest movement around an area. The natural English wording depends on whether the context emphasizes a place, a route, or being casually out.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Salimos por ahí después de cenar.",
        "en": "We went out and about after dinner."
      },
      "tags": ["phrase", "location", "informal", "A2"]
    }
